    <outcome date="2026-10-01" branch="task/uac-r2-141-f1" round="verifier-fix">
BLOCKED ON AN OWNER DECISION (finding 1); every other finding closed. Full record: notes/task-141-identity-binding.md §9 (the escalation), §10 (per finding), §10.1 (seeded violations), §11 (PR statements).

FINDING 1 (CRITICAL, alternate key vs FLS on contact.sprk_externalobjectid): confirmed against Microsoft Learn ("Attributes must not have field-level security applied"; "Columns that have the Enable column security property enabled can't be used as an alternate key"). NOT decided here — an unanswered escalation is a first-class stop. Options A/B1/B2/C/D with costs in notes §9; recommendation B2 (keep FLS on the binding column; alternate key on a new unsecured mirror column written with it; reads unchanged; tampering with the mirror can only deny service). Done instead: Set-ContactIdentityBindingSchema.ps1 gained a platform-rule preflight that stops -Apply before any network call (shown to bite: throws BLOCKED with the overlap; a temp copy without it proceeds to authentication) and reports FAIL in dry run / -Verify. The in-memory store's doc states it models a combination the platform refuses. Link contract §1.1, guide §6.5.2, the provisioning handoff, SPA-r2 023 closure and its delivery note corrected. Criteria 3 and FLS stay open on this decision.

FINDING 2 (four guards never shown to bite): tests added and each seeded alone — truncated scan (F1), probe Failed (F2), cheap Verified path IsActive (F3), invite-flag re-evaluation (F4, pure + job). All RED when seeded, restored.

FINDING 3 (one flag per contact): fixed for systemuser AND token-plane parties. A flag records every colliding party (CollisionParty; new memo column sprk_identitycollisionparties, JSON; the four summary columns remain the first party). Idempotence per party (identity + reason): a retry writes nothing, a different identity is appended. Job pass 2 evaluates each party and applies the pure ContactBindingDecision.ReconcileFlag: clear only when no party holds AND no systemuser collided with the contact this run (the verifier's rule); prune otherwise. Appends, prunes and clears are conditional on the row version (412 on an append re-reads once and appends again; a prune or clear without a version is refused). A flag at 20 parties or with an unreadable parties column is never overwritten or cleared by the job; the operator clears it after resolving (guide §6.5.3). Seeds F5-F9, F11, F12.

FINDING 4 (inline link ungated): WorkforcePrincipalResolver.TryLinkSystemUserAsync now does nothing (no read, no write) unless IdentityLink:Reconciliation:WritesEnabled is true, the job's own switch, read through ContactIdentityBinder.LinkWritesEnabled (the job uses the same helper). Not gated, with reasons in the binder doc and guide §6.5.2: the Type-2 first sign-in and the registration link. Seed F10.

FINDING 5: the D-3 mixing (a flagged kept link honoured by IdentityNormalizationService, so AccessibleRecordSetService loads that contact's external grants for the licensed user — Ralph in dev) is stated for the PR in notes §11 and in the link contract §5.

FINDING 13 (acct): re-checked READ-ONLY — az ad app show --id 1e40baad-e065-4aea-a8d4-4b7ab273458c: access-token optional claims email, preferred_username, upn; acct NOT configured; AzureADMultipleOrgs; v1 tokens. The Teams package's webApplicationInfo.id is this registration. Microsoft documents acct for JWT v1.0/v2.0 and that access-token optional claims apply to every access token issued for the API, Teams SSO included. Trigger 3 does not fire. App registration not changed (G-2 pending), dev setting not set (G-3 pending).

FINDINGS 6, 7, 9: nothing to fix (023 status kept as POML step 10 asked, with a status-note that it is delivered but not live). FINDINGS 8, 15: publish size not measured (instructed). FINDINGS 10-12, 14: see 1, 3, and §8 (G-5 counts no longer drift).

PLACEMENT / JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md §10/§11): no new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or package. New surface: the memo column sprk_identitycollisionparties with the CollisionParty / FlagReconciliation types (extends CollisionFlag and the four flag columns; a text(100) oid column cannot hold a list; cost of nothing = finding 3), and the static helper ContactIdentityBinder.LinkWritesEnabled (the job's existing parse, shared; cost of nothing = finding 4). WorkforcePrincipalResolver gains an IConfiguration constructor dependency (already registered). All in the BFF per bff-extensions.md §A.

TESTS: identity-binding set (IdentityBinding, WorkforceEmailNoHijack, DataverseContactIdentityStore, ExternalAccessContractTests, RegistrationContactLink, WorkforcePrincipalResolver) 228 passed / 0 failed; full BFF suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests) 13,368 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (13,422); NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests) 337 / 0 / 0. ADR-038: no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration test, no ctor null-check test; no InternalsVisibleTo used by the new tests.

LIVE: nothing was written to Dataverse, Entra or Azure. Read-only: the az ad app show above; the schema-script guard proof used an invalid URL and stopped before any request.
