    <outcome date="2026-10-01" branch="task/uac-r2-141-f2" round="verifier-fix-2">
STILL BLOCKED ON THE OWNER DECISION in notes §9 (alternate key vs FLS on contact.sprk_externalobjectid; recommendation B2). Findings 4, 5 and 6 fixed; 7 and 8 recorded; 1-3 and 11-15 are the §9 decision and the pending manual gates G-1..G-9, unchanged. Full record: notes/task-141-identity-binding.md §12 (per finding), §12.1 (recorded gap), §12.2 (PR statements), §12.3 (seeded violations), §12.4 (placement), §12.5 (suites).

FINDING 4 (registration link promised a retry that does not exist outside the BFF's own environment): RegistrationDataverseService.IsReconciledByThisBff compares the link environment with Dataverse:ServiceUrl, the only environment IdentityLinkReconciliationJob scans. A link that does not land logs one of two warnings: "re-decides the user on its next run once IdentityLink:Reconciliation:WritesEnabled is true" (own environment) or "NOT retried by this BFF" (any other). XML doc, the binder's Failed-outcome doc, its link-not-written log line and its switch remarks corrected. RECORDED GAP (notes §12.1, guide §6.5.2, link contract §3), not a retry: a registration link in another environment is covered only by a BFF deployed against that environment; a safety net (bounded retry, or a registry-scanning job) is an owner choice not taken here. Seeds S1, S2.

FINDING 5 (invite lookup failure lost its reason code): InviteContactAction.Fail now returns InviteLookupFailure → HTTP 503 ProblemDetails, reasonCode sdap.access.invite.contact_lookup_failed, detail = ContactIdentityBinder.InviteMessage (no longer dead), on /invite AND /invite-and-grant; nothing created, bound, flagged or granted. ProducesProblem(503) declared on both. Seeds S3, S4.

FINDING 6 (two answers to one question): ContactBindingDecision.ActiveContactsBoundToQuery renamed ContactsBoundToQuery and widened to every statecode (statecode selected, top 2), matching the binder's FindContactsByOidAsync. IdentityNormalizationService and CallerContactResolver answer it with DecideBoundContact (the binder's own D1-D4 step, made public) over BoundContactLookup. Active + inactive on one oid → no contact in both readers, as in the binder; a sole inactive contact → none (CallerContactResolver reason inactive-contact). Seeds S5-S8.

FINDING 7 (INFO): Ralph's flagged kept link is honoured (D-3, owner I2 = (1)); repeated for the PR in notes §12.2. FINDING 8 (INFO): report-only cost recorded in guide §6.5.2; the later-BU re-run was already documented.

FINDINGS 1, 11 (criterion 3), 2, 12, 13 (FLS + live gate): blocked on §9 / G-1, G-7, G-8. FINDINGS 3, 14: acct re-checked READ-ONLY 2026-10-01 (az ad app show --id 1e40baad-e065-4aea-a8d4-4b7ab273458c: access-token optional claims email, preferred_username, upn; acct NOT configured; AzureADMultipleOrgs; v1) — trigger 3 does not fire; G-2 and G-3 pending; the app registration was not changed. FINDING 15: suites re-run below; publish size G-9 not measured (instructed).

PLACEMENT / JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md §10/§11): no new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, job or package; all in the BFF (bff-extensions.md §A), inside existing components. New public surface (three-question table in notes §12.4): IsReconciledByThisBff (existing: the job's Dataverse:ServiceUrl store; extends RegistrationDataverseService; cost of nothing: operators told a link is retried when it never is); InviteLookupFailure + LookupFailureResult (existing: InviteRefusal + RefusalResult; sibling, since a failure is not a refusal; cost: the reason code never reaches the client); ContactsBoundToQuery / BoundContactLookup / DecideBoundContact (existing: ActiveContactsBoundToQuery, private DecideOnOid; exposes rather than copies; cost: readers and binder disagree); the inactive-contact reason identifier.

TESTS: seeds S1-S8 each RED alone, sources restored byte-identical. ADR-038: no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration test, no ctor null-check test, no InternalsVisibleTo. Identity/access subset 354 passed / 0 failed; full BFF suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests) 13,382 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (13,436); NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests) 337 / 0 / 0. No package or csproj change. Publish size not measured (G-9).

LIVE: nothing written to Dataverse, Entra or Azure; the only live call was the read-only az ad app show.
