    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-141-f3" round="fix-3">
CODE-COMPLETE; OWNER-APPROVED LIVE GATES PENDING (main session). Full record: notes/task-141-identity-binding.md §13 (§13.0 merge, §13.1 B2, §13.2 registration gap, §13.3 other findings, §13.4 placement + justification, §13.5 seeded violations, §13.6 Step 9.5, §13.7 suites); gates in §8 (G-1 unblocked, NEW G-1b). Peer contract notes/141-link-contract.md updated (§1, §1.1, §3, §4, §5, new §7 "what changed for consumers") — ready for word-add-in-r1 task 083.

MERGE: integ/uac-r2-batch2 merged (origin/master + 130/131/134/151 + 109/135/136/144/145). Five conflicts resolved keeping both sides — CiamContactPrincipalStrategy now takes identity from ContactIdentityBinder (141) AND record scope from the unified evaluator (135/136), and no longer depends on ExternalParticipationService; both scheduled jobs registered; the contract-test host carries 136's DataReads stub, 141's identity store and 135/136's veto/plane wiring. Three 135/144 test files that built on the participation service's removed contact resolution or on the pre-141 registration ctor were rewired (no behaviour change). Identity/access subset after the merge 519/0.

(1) OWNER ROUND 4 ITEM 4 = B2, IMPLEMENTED per the notes §9 impact list: FLS stays on contact.sprk_externalobjectid; the alternate key sprk_ExternalObjectIdUniqueKey sits on the new unsecured mirror contact.sprk_externalobjectidkey (Text 100). BindPayload writes binding + mirror + plane in one request; CreatePayload(oid, ...) carries the binding; BuildCreateByKeyPath addresses the mirror; every read (store, ContactsBoundToQuery, both read-only readers) still filters on the secured column. The duplicate-key fault (0x80060892, HTTP 412) is classified StoreWriteStatus.KeyConflict, never retried as a version race; a bind refused by the index, or a create refused twice with no contact bound, flags the holder (new reason KeyMirrorConflict 100000011) and denies sdap.access.deny.contact_key_conflict — a squatted mirror DENIES, never binds (tests on the workforce, CIAM, systemuser and job paths). The flag holds while the mirror slot is held, even on an inactive holder, and is judged from the holder row (so a report-only run never promises to clear it). InMemoryContactIdentityStore models the key on the mirror and no longer a key+FLS combination the platform refuses. Schema script: step (a) creates the mirror and copies the 6 existing bindings into it before step (b) keys it; platform-rule preflight PASSES (shown: -Apply against an unreachable URL passes the preflight and stops at auth; a seeded copy with the key back on the binding throws BLOCKED before any request; read-only dry run on spaarkedev1: OK, 6 copies WOULD, key WOULD); new source guard ContactIdentitySchemaAgreementTests (script keys exactly KeyMirrorColumn, secures the binding, never both on one column, choices cover every enum value). Link contract §1.1 and guide §6.5.2/§6.5.3 rewritten. CRITERION 3 (exactly one contact per oid under two concurrent first sign-ins) IS MET in code, platform-enforced once G-1 creates the key.

(2) REGISTRATION-LINK GAP CLOSED (not recorded): IdentityLinkReconciliationJob now reconciles, after its own environment, every environment this BFF provisions users into — DATAVERSE_URL and every ACTIVE sprk_dataverseenvironment row (ProvisioningTargetUrls: normalised, de-duplicated, never the own environment) — with the full probe, pass 1 and pass 2 through RegistrationDataverseService.ContactBinderFor(url), the existing per-environment token path. Same report-only switch everywhere; one environment's failure fails the run but never the others; an unreadable registry fails the run while DATAVERSE_URL is still reconciled. Because the approve endpoint provisions only into ACTIVE registry rows (and the default is DATAVERSE_URL), every registration-created user is in an environment the job reconciles: a failed link is retried and a flag written there is re-evaluated and cleared. IsReconciledByThisBff and the "NOT retried" warning are gone. LIVE FINDING (read-only): the dev BFF's only provisioning target is Demo 1 (spaarke-demo), where the dev BFF identities are NOT application users and the binding schema does not exist — every run will report that environment as failed (accurately; registration from dev into Demo 1 cannot work either). New decision G-1b for the main session/owner (not covered by round 4's approval, which named dev): (a) add the dev BFF MI as an app user there and run G-1 against it, (b) deactivate the stale Demo 1 registry row in spaarkedev1 (recommended), or (c) accept the reported failure during G-5/G-6.

(3) OTHER VERDICT FINDINGS: INFO 503-detail test fixed (the endpoint's last-resort fallback text is now distinct and the test pins the decision's InviteMessage). Remaining verdict items are live gates (FLS authorization, manual live gate, acct claim, dev tenant setting, publish size) — owner-approved, run by the main session.

ESCALATION TRIGGERS: none fired. Round-4 answers in force; no ADR tension (Step 9.5 below).

PLACEMENT / JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md §10/§11): no new service, DI registration, endpoint, option, scheduled job or package; all in the BFF (bff-extensions.md §A) inside existing components — the existing job gains a pass, the existing store/binder/decision gain members. Three-question table per new surface in notes §13.4: the mirror column + key + reason option (owner-decided; the binding cannot carry the key; without it every create denies), KeyMirrorColumn / MirrorHeldWithoutBinding / DenyContactKeyConflict / KeyMirrorConflict / RawKeyMirror (extend the decision; without them a squat is indistinguishable from a race), StoreWriteStatus.KeyConflict / IsDuplicateKey / FindContactsByKeyMirrorAsync (extend the store; without them a duplicate-key 412 is retried as a race and the holder cannot be flagged), RegistrationDataverseService.ContactBinderFor (extracts the existing token path so the job reuses it, ADR-028), the job's provisioning-target pass + ProvisioningTargetUrls (extends the existing job; without it the verifier's gap stays open), DataverseEnvironmentService.GetActiveEnvironmentsAsync virtual (test seam; ADR-038 B1). ADR-052/ADR-036: no new background work; the existing AddScheduledJob registration is unchanged.

STEP 9.5: code-review + adr-check over the diff. ADR-002/003/010/028/036/038/052 compliant; no tension. Fixed from review: per-environment status in the heartbeat and ResultJson; an unreachable environment no longer reported as "masked"; a test helper no longer sets a key the service stopped reading. Accepted with reasons (notes §13.6): a repeated squatted sign-in costs two refused creates + five reads + one error log (idempotent flag); the job file grew (~700 lines) but keeps one reason to change; dev reports spaarke-demo failed until G-1b.

SEEDED VIOLATIONS: B1-B20 each seeded alone, built, run, restored byte-identical and touched — all RED (notes §13.5; B16/B19/B20 re-run with a harness that rebuilds before every run).

TESTS: identity/access subset 637 passed / 0 failed; full BFF suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests) 13,791 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (13,845); NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests) 341 / 0 / 0. ADR-038: no Mock of HttpMessageHandler, no DI-registration test, no ctor null-check test, no InternalsVisibleTo. No package or csproj change. Publish size not measured (G-9, main session).

LIVE (read-only only): schema dry run against spaarkedev1; sprk_dataverseenvironment rows in spaarkedev1; application users and binding columns in spaarke-demo; az webapp config appsettings list filtered to DATAVERSE_URL and Dataverse__ServiceUrl. Nothing written to Dataverse, Entra or Azure.
